pe":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"C045\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"Covers pro-rata proceeds ('pro-rata share of the fund's net assets'). Says the amount may differ from the last price ('not automatically... the latest quoted share price'). Says timing varies ('timing varies; check the fund's liquidation notice'). Notes 'Trading may stop before the fund distributes cash' but never says the investor can normally sell before trading ends, so the bundle is incomplete.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States proceeds are 'after liabilities and liquidation costs'. Says that in a taxable account 'the cash distribution generally triggers a taxable gain or loss measured against your adjusted cost basis', and mentions possible pass-through of gains.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"There is no central error. The answer explicitly says liquidation does not ordinarily mean forfeiting the whole holding, and it gives no fixed proceeds or date. Point 2 is fully covered. Point 1 lacks the minimum element that investors can normally sell before trading ends. Required coverage is 1.5 of 2, which meets the partial threshold but not correct.\"}","ttft_ms":3509,"type":"result","duration_ms":6750,"uuid":"5482eece-e8d5-4510-8cf1-760fd1b3b728","ttft_stream_ms":1430,"time_to_request_ms":66,"first_content_frame_ms":1430,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
